<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Helier de Carteret</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1532–<a href="/years/1581">1581</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Helier de Carteret was a Jersey nobleman, Seigneur of Saint Ouen, who colonised the Channel Island of Sark. In 1565 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i">Elizabeth I</a> granted him the island as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fief">fief</a> on condition that he keep it settled with at least forty men able to defend it against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piracy">pirates</a> and the French. He divided Sark into forty holdings, laying the foundations of its feudal constitution, which lasted until 2008.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/helier-de-carteret.jpg" alt="Helier de Carteret" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andrewrabbott · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Memorial_to_Helier_de_Carteret_in_St_Peter%27s_Church,_Sark.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Sark in the Channel Islands, settled in 1565 by <b>Helier de Carteret</b> under a charter from Elizabeth I and divided into forty tenements whose holders sat in its parliament, kept what was called Europe’s last feudal system until 2008.</blockquote><a href="/government/feudalism">Feudalism · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1565 Elizabeth I granted it as a fief to <b>Helier de Carteret</b> of Jersey, on condition that he settle it with at least forty men to defend it.</blockquote><a href="/state/sark">Sark</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Saint Ouen. Died in Saint Ouen. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=49.24,-2.22&amp;year=1563" aria-label="Saint Ouen on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4499 447 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Helier de Carteret"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4949 717h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4949 717h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=49.24,-2.22&amp;year=1563">What was here in 1563? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
